# Trivy suppressions. Each entry needs, on the line above it:
#   reason (why it does not apply or cannot be fixed yet), owner, review date (YYYY-MM-DD).
# Example:
#   # CVE-2026-00000: dev-only dependency, not in the runtime image. Owner: Osoba 4. Review: 2026-12-01
#   CVE-2026-00000
# Prefer fixing (upgrade, remove the package, change the base image) over suppressing.

# Caddy 2.11.7 (edge and web images) is the latest 2.11 release and is built with Go 1.26.8; the fixes
# are in Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2 and no Caddy image with them exists yet. All four are denial of service
# (HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames, Range headers, TLS ECH extension), none gives code execution or data access.
# Owner: repository owner (B-17). Review: 2026-11-01, or as soon as a Caddy image built with Go >= 1.26.9
# appears; then bump the image in infra/docker-compose.yml and app/Dockerfile and delete these lines.
